Docker Commands
=======================================
-Docker Info==>Displaying info about the running one 
-Docker --help ==>List all the docker commands with descriptions
-Docker images ==>List all images that exists 
-Docker pull [imageName]==>Downloading the image from the DockerHub
-Docker rmi [imageId]==>Deleting the image using image id returned form [Docker images] command
-Docker login==>Login 

-Docker ps ==>List only Running Containers now
-Docker run [imageName]==>Create Container from the existing image if the image is not downloaded the command will download it first and
create the contaier next, But not start it only create the container 
-Docker start [containerId]==>Start the container run it (If you have the Container id from [Docker ps] command )
-Docker run -it [imageName]==>create new container and Start Running the Container and interacting with it
-Docker stop [containerId]==>Stop the container 
-Docker rm [containerId]==>Remove the container 
